# Vercel Web Analytics Installation Report

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for this Next.js portfolio project.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/analytics` package (version automatically resolved by npm)
- Updated `package.json` with the new dependency
- Updated `package-lock.json` with dependency tree (376 packages added)

### 2. Analytics Configuration
Modified `app/layout.tsx`:
- Added import statement: `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next"`
- Added `<Analytics />` component inside the `<body>` element after `{children}`

## Implementation Details

### Framework-Specific Setup
This project uses Next.js 16.3.5 with the App Router, so I followed the official Vercel documentation for Next.js App Router setup:
1. Fetched the latest installation instructions from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart
2. Installed the package using npm (the project's package manager)
3. Added the Analytics component to the root layout file as per Next.js App Router guidelines

### File Changes
**Created:**
- None

**Modified:**
- `app/layout.tsx` - Added Analytics import and component
- `package.json` - Added @vercel/analytics dependency
- `package-lock.json` - Updated with new dependency tree

## Verification Steps Completed
✓ Linter passed without errors (`npm run lint`)
✓ Build completed successfully (`npm run build`)
✓ All dependencies installed correctly
✓ TypeScript compilation successful
✓ No tests to run (no test script defined in package.json)

## Next Steps
To activate Web Analytics on Vercel:
1. Deploy this project to Vercel (`vercel deploy`)
2. Enable Web Analytics in the Vercel dashboard (Analytics section)
3. Monitor the Network tab for analytics requests confirming data collection

## Notes
- The Analytics component is automatically tree-shaken in development mode
- Analytics will only track data when deployed on Vercel
- No additional configuration is required; the component works out of the box
- The implementation follows the latest official Vercel documentation guidelines
